# Build artifacts
**/zig-out/
**/.zig-cache/
*.o
*.tar

# Staged candidate solution (created by harness/run.py --solution).
# run.py resets solution/candidate/ each run and stages only allowlisted
# source. reference/ (the gen_tests.py oracle) is tracked separately.
tasks/*/solution/candidate/

# Test reports (generated per-run)
**/report.json

# Work directories (agent output): work/<task>-<run_id>/ holds ~KB of agent
# source plus ~GB of trajectory.jsonl streaming partials, .zig-cache/, and
# compiled binaries. Never tracked. Source worth keeping is extracted to
# sessions/ by harness/archive.py (which uses the same source filter as grading).
work/

# Archived agent code: sessions/<task>/<run_id>/. Track ONLY source the agent
# wrote (*.c/.h/.zig/.nim/.v/.zon/.rs/.go, Makefile, build.zig) — extracted by
# harness/archive.py from the full work dir. Everything else the agent left
# behind (trajectories, caches, binaries, *.bin fixtures, scratch) is gitignored
# so a stray copy never bloats the repo. Mirrors source_filter.
#
# Mechanism (a git gotcha): once a directory is ignored, git won't descend, so
# file-level un-ignores never match. The fix is to un-ignore the directory tree
# (slash-terminated `!sessions/**/`) so git traverses it, then un-ignore source
# by extension. Cruft patterns at the bottom keep the rest ignored.
sessions/**
!sessions/**/
!*.c
!*.h
!*.zig
!*.nim
!*.v
!*.zon
!*.rs
!*.go
!Makefile
!build.zig
!build.zig.zon
# Session/work cruft — scoped so Harbor tasks (tasks/*/solution, fixtures, etc.) stay tracked
sessions/**/*.bin
sessions/**/*.o
sessions/**/*.json
sessions/**/trajectory.jsonl
sessions/**/solution
work/**/*.bin
work/**/*.o
work/**/*.json
work/**/trajectory.jsonl
work/**/solution

# Python
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
jobs/
